{
    "word": "избыточно",
    "lang_code": "ru",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [],
        "ru-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "a2c1bfe1-a2a1-39d8-8260-2e5845bfa8c3",
                "word": "избыточно",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "ru",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a5204e4e-e3ad-31aa-aec0-a48170172164",
                        "entry_id": "a2c1bfe1-a2a1-39d8-8260-2e5845bfa8c3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "наречие к избыточный; превышая нужное количество; больше, чем необходимо"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "adverb"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ade7ee4f-36ba-4c83-8621-fe39d9095eac",
                                "sense_id": "a5204e4e-e3ad-31aa-aec0-a48170172164",
                                "text": "Живопись маслом требует единства красок тёплых, а ты вот подвёл избыточно белил, и вышли у богородицы глазки холодные, зимние."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1d2f4f48-25a4-3362-82a6-36de92f18b44",
                        "entry_id": "a2c1bfe1-a2a1-39d8-8260-2e5845bfa8c3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. в большом количестве, в избытке"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "237c2fce-e4f3-4efb-805b-319191729745",
                                "sense_id": "1d2f4f48-25a4-3362-82a6-36de92f18b44",
                                "text": "Обилуя же водою имеет тучные пажити, и избыточно плодятся там коровы, лошади, ослы, ишаки, козы и свиньи…"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "dc9e1b00-5ed5-44dd-922f-346f6693f636",
                        "source_entry_id": "a2c1bfe1-a2a1-39d8-8260-2e5845bfa8c3",
                        "source_sense_description": "превышая нужное количество; больше, чем необходимо",
                        "target_lang_word": "overly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "overly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bc818fd5-0bd4-387b-9142-1bad5f66a6fc",
                                        "entry_id": "6a9d6dc0-a565-3c80-bb36-014c68230810",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To an excessive degree."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "proscribed",
                                            "sometimes"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "efd8f8db-a8c3-4c5a-b942-60ea09a0421e",
                                                "sense_id": "bc818fd5-0bd4-387b-9142-1bad5f66a6fc",
                                                "text": "Parents can be overly protective of their children."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f40a8ee-2532-42b7-9a6c-02859f15be98",
                                                "sense_id": "bc818fd5-0bd4-387b-9142-1bad5f66a6fc",
                                                "text": "[…] considering the circumstances of my situation, I saw it would not do for me to look out for an overly young woman, nor yet would it do for one of my ways to take an elderly maiden, ladies of that sort being liable to possess strong-set particularities."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e76cac6-f305-4e13-8690-760ecff45eca",
                                                "sense_id": "bc818fd5-0bd4-387b-9142-1bad5f66a6fc",
                                                "text": "It’s nothing short of wonderful how she’s improved these three years, but especially in looks. She’s a real pretty girl got to be, though I can’t say I’m overly partial to that pale, big-eyed style myself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02db6706-0f0e-454f-87c2-91b25bc2e25a",
                                                "sense_id": "bc818fd5-0bd4-387b-9142-1bad5f66a6fc",
                                                "text": "Your race is overly sentimental; it distorts your judgment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a034a786-9445-4e00-821b-13d622c75873",
                                                "sense_id": "bc818fd5-0bd4-387b-9142-1bad5f66a6fc",
                                                "text": "This means, at times, long and perhaps overly discursive discussions of other taxa."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f380f8c9-bb1b-4880-8c51-12ac7de00e2e",
                                                "sense_id": "bc818fd5-0bd4-387b-9142-1bad5f66a6fc",
                                                "text": "And this is where the larger problem lies: when states try to enforce impossible bans, everyone loses. 3D printing farragoes have all the hallmarks of the absolute worst kind of ineffectual ban: one which encourages overly draconian laws that carry huge side effects, and that ultimately to have little to no effect."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a26e4de-589e-3b51-af3e-9418edd33d4b",
                                        "entry_id": "6a9d6dc0-a565-3c80-bb36-014c68230810",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To a high degree; very."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "negative",
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5fafce18-d6f4-45d4-832e-38d4e584ce46",
                                                "sense_id": "2a26e4de-589e-3b51-af3e-9418edd33d4b",
                                                "text": "I'm not overly enthusiastic about meeting him."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "37df1877-c011-3c79-813b-cbf90ab5214a",
                                        "entry_id": "6a9d6dc0-a565-3c80-bb36-014c68230810",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Superficially."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "682b0a07-97b3-4e37-8fc5-cb687d7ee2f3",
                                                "sense_id": "37df1877-c011-3c79-813b-cbf90ab5214a",
                                                "text": "1566, Thomas Blundeville, The Fower Chiefyst Offices Belongyng to Horsemanshippe, London, “The true Arte of Paring, and shooyng all maner of Houes together […] ,” Chapter 5,\n[…] let him not touche the quarters nor the heeles at al, vnlesse it be to make the seat of the shoe playne, & let that be done so superficially or ouerly as maye be, so shall the houes remayne alwayes strong."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0411d956-6987-441c-9b0e-71cd0ba151ca",
                                                "sense_id": "37df1877-c011-3c79-813b-cbf90ab5214a",
                                                "text": "These kinds of reproofes, not vnfitly may be compared to hotte or hastie healing salues, which drawe a faire skinne ouer a fowle wound; which because it is not soundly cured from the bottome, but ouerly healed vp, doth afterward apostemate or fistulate, and becommeth more dangerous and desperate then euer before."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a2ac34f-24ba-48d0-8e1e-781b335f4499",
                                                "sense_id": "37df1877-c011-3c79-813b-cbf90ab5214a",
                                                "text": "1678, George Mackenzie, The Laws and Customes of Scotland, in Matters Criminal, Edinburgh, Part 1, “Some Crimes punished amongst the Romans, which are not directly in use with us,” p. 347,\n[…] I resolved here to touch overly even those crimes which are little considered among us, not only that we might thereby know the genius of that wise Nation; but that we may consider how far it were fit to renew amongst us these excellent Laws."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6f00dbcc-ccd2-3879-8cfe-23e78861251b",
                                        "entry_id": "6a9d6dc0-a565-3c80-bb36-014c68230810",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Carelessly, without due attention."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6760e72-464a-4674-9c48-90309ee4c0fb",
                                                "sense_id": "6f00dbcc-ccd2-3879-8cfe-23e78861251b",
                                                "text": "[…] you shall finde this, that all remissenesse, when a man doth a thing remissely, and ouerly, and perfunctorily, it argues alway a diuided intention, it is an argument that the whole minde is not set on it, but that the intention is distracted, and bestowed on other things:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e68fd6c-9bdb-4d73-b24a-90e78b5feb30",
                                                "sense_id": "6f00dbcc-ccd2-3879-8cfe-23e78861251b",
                                                "text": "If you expect the Poor should work cheaper, and not perform their Work slighter and more overly, as we call it, and superficially, you expect what is not in the Nature of the Thing."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ad1c7b33-0a58-33ee-add2-9ca865419ca6",
                                        "entry_id": "6a9d6dc0-a565-3c80-bb36-014c68230810",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "With a sense of superiority, haughtily."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "644ee2be-b5d2-427e-8362-92e678df80a1",
                                                "sense_id": "ad1c7b33-0a58-33ee-add2-9ca865419ca6",
                                                "text": "The third [vice] is Arrogancie, and the fourth Pride, two vices neer a kinne, Cosen germans […] when men shall arrogate much unto themselves; looking overly and superciliously upon others."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "overly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c466c608-466f-3195-8155-1f6ca1099614",
                                        "entry_id": "84ef151c-3afb-33c5-8aff-fc9ae00979bb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Superficial; not thorough; careless, negligent, inattentive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd29c27e-0244-4bdb-b7ea-547863986917",
                                                "sense_id": "c466c608-466f-3195-8155-1f6ca1099614",
                                                "text": "The curteous Citizen bad me to his feast,\nWith hollow words, and ouerly request:\nCome, will ye dine with me this Holy day?\nI yeelded, tho he hop’d I would say Nay:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e071644-8662-4c0a-9932-d5bfc48e361a",
                                                "sense_id": "c466c608-466f-3195-8155-1f6ca1099614",
                                                "text": "Hee prayeth but with an ouerly desire, and not from the deepe of his heart, that will not bend his endeauours withall to obtaine what he desireth:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3932259f-d401-4b3f-b079-3255e2dcc26b",
                                                "sense_id": "c466c608-466f-3195-8155-1f6ca1099614",
                                                "text": "Concerning the passions in particular, however irregular, headstrong, and perverse, in an overly view, they may appear, I propose to show, that they are by nature adjusted and tempered with admirable wisdom, for the good of society as well as for private good."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "51507d4a-954c-3703-9dc3-411ab9e73054",
                                        "entry_id": "84ef151c-3afb-33c5-8aff-fc9ae00979bb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having a sense of superiority, haughty."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "707d9e42-685f-4de8-98ca-3c7e601ad45d",
                                                "sense_id": "51507d4a-954c-3703-9dc3-411ab9e73054",
                                                "text": "Those that know no better, may rejoyce and exult in these worldly contentments; but those, who have had but a blink of the beauty of heaven, can look upon them no otherwise, than with an overly contemptuousnesse."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "679ec42b-e340-3c6e-90f4-1008d441d158",
                                        "entry_id": "84ef151c-3afb-33c5-8aff-fc9ae00979bb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Excessive; too great."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8425ed1f-c0e5-4d10-be36-a1b6d4a951ee",
                                                "sense_id": "679ec42b-e340-3c6e-90f4-1008d441d158",
                                                "text": "[…] there appears a very chilling want of open-heartedness on the part of Owen, produced perhaps by the somewhat overly and certainly most ungracious resentments of Baxter."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "25f42db0-cb25-4313-8f02-5ce9e10ebdcd",
                        "source_entry_id": "a2c1bfe1-a2a1-39d8-8260-2e5845bfa8c3",
                        "source_sense_description": "превышая нужное количество; больше, чем необходимо",
                        "target_lang_word": "overmuch",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "overmuch",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "22f95197-18be-3cda-990c-cbccbfdcb928",
                                        "entry_id": "438ff14d-0ef5-35e2-93ec-37cf74ee2646",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Very much; too much; overly much."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89794a38-8b98-4c98-acf5-cf31846c375c",
                                                "sense_id": "22f95197-18be-3cda-990c-cbccbfdcb928",
                                                "text": "So that contrariwise ye ought rather to forgive him, and comfort him, lest perhaps such a one should be swallowed up with overmuch sorrow."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80d363ca-6dff-499f-abe8-72f5a687ff94",
                                                "sense_id": "22f95197-18be-3cda-990c-cbccbfdcb928",
                                                "text": "If we met with accidents, such as losing canoes and men in the rapids, or losing men in encounters with Indians, or if we encountered overmuch fever and dysentery, the loads would lighten themselves."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7a211f7-9308-49c1-ba7a-30b4412ddc9d",
                                                "sense_id": "22f95197-18be-3cda-990c-cbccbfdcb928",
                                                "text": "He had much prudence, much conscientiousness, and there were occasions when these virtues were the cause of overmuch disquietude in him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1586e6e8-7591-47d6-8cd8-0f6538105b7b",
                                                "sense_id": "22f95197-18be-3cda-990c-cbccbfdcb928",
                                                "text": "This seemed to me a more important priority in 1959 than overmuch argument about nuclear philosophical heresies of one kind or another."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "overmuch",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "34364dbd-f82f-3918-90b2-22347ca42c24",
                                        "entry_id": "d337328d-8102-31be-adff-914b835ba85a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Excessive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e47318a-3cc7-4d40-8386-c508476bdb82",
                                                "sense_id": "34364dbd-f82f-3918-90b2-22347ca42c24",
                                                "text": "[…]it is good to be applyed to womens breaſts, that grow ſore by the aboundance of milke comming into them: as alſo to repreſſe the overmuch bleeding of the hemorrhoids, to coole the Inflammations of the parts thereabouts, and to give eaſe of paines:[…]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c914a01-b0b0-4f3d-9216-eb638de78748",
                                                "sense_id": "34364dbd-f82f-3918-90b2-22347ca42c24",
                                                "text": "Our Palates like the Seaſoning and Cookery they are ſet to, and an over much Uſe of Salt, beſides that it occaſions thirſt, and over-much Drinking, has other ill Effects upon the Body."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "overmuch",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d1ba11d1-a08a-3c46-a9da-23429fa84ed0",
                                        "entry_id": "8cac83c5-f10f-331a-90b6-16d97e1354a9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Too much; overly much"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "549e72c6-a996-410b-9598-fa0a5cd94ffc",
                                                "sense_id": "d1ba11d1-a08a-3c46-a9da-23429fa84ed0",
                                                "text": "Some readers do not care overmuch for poetry."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1df81f86-50d1-4c16-8e7e-5eddbd73a45d",
                                                "sense_id": "d1ba11d1-a08a-3c46-a9da-23429fa84ed0",
                                                "text": "O, he hath kept an evil diet long, / And overmuch consumed his royal person:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff114bbf-48b1-4d05-9ef3-5435c1b8cc79",
                                                "sense_id": "d1ba11d1-a08a-3c46-a9da-23429fa84ed0",
                                                "text": "Be not righteous over much; neither make thyself over wise: why shouldest thou destroy thyself?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc9bc22b-5a32-477d-8b57-cff820a6312e",
                                                "sense_id": "d1ba11d1-a08a-3c46-a9da-23429fa84ed0",
                                                "text": "\"[…] Do you be humble, and tempt you the Big Man not overmuch. He is quick to anger.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b0f0291-9462-498a-b54d-b7bf6c9440ad",
                                                "sense_id": "d1ba11d1-a08a-3c46-a9da-23429fa84ed0",
                                                "text": "yet what am i that such and such / mysteries very simple touch / me,whose heart-wholeness overmuch / Expects of your hair pale, / a terror musical?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eec41168-1bc3-41cc-a28f-90be0ad68141",
                                                "sense_id": "d1ba11d1-a08a-3c46-a9da-23429fa84ed0",
                                                "text": "All of us were being paid regularly, wined and dined overmuch and had the whole theater world of Moscow for our enjoyment."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "overmuch",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b615a991-6744-36bd-bee6-ac88b5773f8f",
                                        "entry_id": "f0ef1372-eeb7-3241-bedb-9df21f8965e7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An excessive amount; too much."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e5216ec-40db-4224-8493-aabf3bd679ee",
                                                "sense_id": "b615a991-6744-36bd-bee6-ac88b5773f8f",
                                                "text": "They had felled too freely here; the sawmills had taken over-much, leaving next to no young wood."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62c66e7b-a182-4318-81f6-56d475257dc8",
                                                "sense_id": "b615a991-6744-36bd-bee6-ac88b5773f8f",
                                                "text": "If citizens hear overmuch of the bliss of others, it galls the secrecy of their hearts."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
